.TH ISA-PREFLIGHT 8 "November 2026" "isa-preflight 0.1" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
isa-preflight \- verify processor features or chain-load an init program
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B isa-preflight
is an executable intended to run as the first userspace program in an
initramfs. On x86-64 variant builds, it checks the CPU flags of every processor
reported in
.I /proc/cpuinfo
and mounts
.I /proc
if necessary, unmounting it again before the handoff. If a required flag is missing, it reports the missing features
and halts the system. If all checks pass, it executes the configured successor
with its original arguments and environment.
.PP
The architecture variant and its required flags are compiled into the
executable. Variant builds are freestanding and static. When built without a
variant, the executable is dynamically linked, skips CPU checking, and only
chain-loads the configured successor. The executable does not contain a
distribution-specific init path.
.SH BUILD-TIME CONFIGURATION
.TP
.I DEB_HOST_ARCH_VARIANT
Selects the architecture variant during a package build. An empty value builds
a generic dynamically linked no-op chainloader on every architecture. Nonempty variant
builds currently support x86-64.
.TP
.I -Dvariant=VARIANT
Selects the variant for direct Meson builds.
.TP
.I VARIANTTABLE
Specifies dpkg's variant table during a package build, defaulting to
.IR /usr/share/dpkg/varianttable .
The selected row supplies the variant name and comma-separated Linux CPU flags.
For direct Meson builds, use
.IR -Dvarianttable=PATH .
.SH RUNTIME CONFIGURATION
The configuration directory is
.IR /etc/isa-preflight .
.TP
.I next-init
A single line containing the absolute path of the executable to run after a
successful check. The original argument vector, including
.IR argv[0] ,
and environment are passed unchanged, so the successor sees the name it was
started as (normally
.IR /init ).
LF and CRLF line endings are accepted.
.SH DRACUT INTEGRATION
The package installs
.IR /usr/lib/dracut/modules.d/99preinit/module-setup.sh .
The late module is included automatically when the preflight executable is
available, so installing or removing the package enables or disables the
integration without modifying dracut. The module runs after dracut's init
providers, saves the handoff path in
.IR next-init ,
and installs the preflight executable as
.IR /init .
.PP
Installation, upgrades, and removal activate the
.B update-initramfs
trigger to refresh existing images according to the installed generator's update
policy. Separately managed images must be regenerated by their image builder.
.PP
A symlinked init is replaced with a handoff directly to its resolved target;
a regular init script is preserved as
.IR /init.dracut .
Symlink chains, including absolute links and links in parent directories, are
resolved inside the image rather than against the build host.
When
.B squash-lib
is included, only its outer loader is wrapped and the inner init is unchanged.
The non-variant executable's dynamic loader and libraries are installed into the
same root as the executable, including the outer root when squash is used.
.TP
.I DRACUT_PREINIT
An absolute path overriding the preflight executable while generating an
initramfs. By default the module uses
.IR /usr/lib/isa-preflight/isa-preflight .
.SH EXIT BEHAVIOR
A successful check does not return: the successor replaces
.B isa-preflight
via
.BR execve (2).
Configuration errors and unsupported processors cause a diagnostic followed by
a system halt when running as PID 1. When running with another PID, or if
halting is unavailable, the program pauses indefinitely.
.SH NOTES
The x86-64 variant checker is freestanding and compiled for the base x86-64
instruction set so that its own instructions do not require the variant being
checked.
